body:
Some of the benefits of this are:
- Validator message processing is not blocked by HTTP API block produce requests anymore;
- Less message sending between services;
- Less code in validator (block producing belongs in beacon node side anyway);
- Easier refactoring and parallelization of block producing code in the future.

Risc0 have deprecated bonsai API, so proving updated to request proofs
from boundless network. Currently proof verification is not implemented,
as there is no documentation on how to verify proof offchain.

Command-line arguments take precedence over the file per option;
e.g. lists are replaced, not merged. This behaviour seems to be
consistent with other consensus clients with this feature.

Fixed plugin, after updating Nethermind to 1.39.1 version. Specifically,
following fixes were applied:

  * Bumped Autofac dependency to `9.3.1`;
  * Fixed versioned hashes conversion - new Nethermind version accepts
    `Hash256?[]` instead of `byte[][]`, for engine_newPayloadV{3,4}
    methods.
